    "text": "To find the coefficient of \\(x^2\\) in the expression \\(3(x^2 - x^3) + 2(x - 2x^2 + 3x^5) - (4x^3 - x^2)\\), we will first expand and simplify the expression step by step.\n\n1. **Expand each term in the expression:**\n   \\[\n   3(x^2 - x^3) = 3x^2 - 3x^3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2(x - 2x^2 + 3x^5) = 2x - 4x^2 + 6x^5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -(4x^3 - x^2) = -4x^3 + x^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Combine all the expanded terms:**\n   \\[\n   3x^2 - 3x^3 + 2x - 4x^2 + 6x^5 - 4x^3 + x^2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Group the like terms together:**\n   \\[\n   (3x^2 - 4x^2 + x^2) + (-3x^3 - 4x^3) + 2x + 6x^5\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the like terms:**\n   \\[\n   (3x^2 - 4x^2 + x^2) = 0x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (-3x^3 - 4x^3) = -7x^3\n   \\]\n\n5. **Write the simplified expression:**\n   \\[\n   -7x^3 + 2x + 6x^5\n   \\]\n\n6. **Identify the coefficient of \\(x^2\\):**\n   In the simplified expression \\(-7x^3 + 2x + 6x^5\\), there is no \\(x^2\\) term. Therefore, the coefficient of \\(x^2\\) is \\(0\\).\n\nThus, the coefficient of \\(x^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).",
